lled journals delegate patch application through `apply` and must not record that navigation again as a new external edit."},"3041":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method     | Purpose                                                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rebase()` | Keep current state and discard all past/future history. |","table":"table-3"},"3042":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method                                | Purpose                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `replaceStateWithoutHistory(updater)` | State-owning only: update state, clear history, establish a new baseline. |","table":"table-3"},"3043":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method                                 | Purpose                                                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pauseTracking()` / `resumeTracking()` | State-owning only: apply untracked updates around a new baseline. |","table":"table-3"},"3044":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"Use these methods deliberately; they change what future undo and reset operations can reach."},"3045":{"id":"/docs/reference/in