portant-exported-types","content":"| Type                | Purpose                                          |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PatchableInput<T>` | Best-effort static constraint for durable input. |","table":"table-0"},"3126":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"The `F`, `A`, and `P` parameters track auto-freeze, archive mode, and patch format so capability-specific methods appear only where valid. Prefer inference at application boundaries and name simpler aliases for your own APIs."},"3127":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#durable-input-checks","content":"`PatchableInput<T>` uses finite-depth recursive checking so recursive interfaces remain usable. Broad or `any`-like types cannot prove runtime contents, and TypeScript’s `number` cannot exclude `NaN`, infinities, or `-0`. Keep runtime validation at untrusted boundaries."},"3128":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#read-only-views","content":"`getHistory()` returns `readonly ReadonlyState<S>[]`; observer state and patch views are also read-only. These types describe shared caches and borrowed event values, not an invitation to cast and mutate."},"3129":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#read-only-views","content":"`getControls()` and journal facades are frozen in every build. Their narrow types help prevent accidental state ownership from leaking into presentational components."},"3130":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#open-event-names","content":"`TravelsEvent['type']` accepts known names plus future strings. Do not use an exhaustive `never` assertion that would break after a minor release adds an event:"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#package-declarations","content":"The package exposes development and default ESM builds, CommonJS defaults and declarations, UMD, and types through its export map. Use a current TypeScript module-resolution mode that understands package exports, such as `bundler`, `node16`, or `nodenext`, according to your application."},"3132":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#package-declarations","content":"The source-generated Type Alias Reference contains the exact generic constraints and return shapes for this release."},"3133":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing","content":"Set up the repository, make focused changes, and validate a contribution."},"3135":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#development-setup","content":"Development Setup"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Pull Request Expectations"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#compatibility","content":"Compatibility"},"