},"3189":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"For a major release that changes the factory or restore boundary, publish in dependency order:"},"3190":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-11","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Finish every Travels gate in this checklist and publish `travels@3` from the exact tested artifact."},"3191":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-12","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Install the published core in clean `use-travel` and `zustand-travel` checkouts. Raise their `mutative` peer and development ranges to the range Travels requires (`^2.0.0` for Travels 3), update their lockfiles to the published versions, and rerun each repository's types, tests, production build, and package smoke test."},"3192":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-13","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Publish the binding majors only after those published-core runs pass."},"3193":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-14","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"In a clean consumer, install all three published packages together with `mutative@2`, confirm the install reports no peer dependency conflict, and smoke test a new timeline plus an atomically restored timeline."},"3194":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-15","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Local sibling links are useful candidate evidence, but they do not replace the published-package checks in steps 2 and 4. Do not tag a binding release that requires an unpublished core version."},"3195":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-16","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Push `main`, then create and push a matching release tag:"},"3196":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-17","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"The tag must match the `package.json` version exactly, with a leading `v`."},"3197":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-18","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"The release job picks the npm dist-tag itself: a version above the published `latest` becomes `latest`, a prerelease becomes `next`, and a maintenance release of an older major becomes `v<major>-latest` (for example `v2-latest`), so it never replaces the current major."},"3198":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-19","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Confirm the tag-triggered release flow completed:"},"3199":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-20","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"`Release`"},"3200":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-21","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"`API Docs`, dispatched by `Release` with the release tag"},"3201":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-22","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Smoke test the published package:"},"3202":{"id":"/docs/resources/security","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"page","content":"Security Policy","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security"},"3203":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security","content":"Supported versions and the responsible vulnerability reporting process."},"3204":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security#supported-versions","content":"Supported Versions"},"3205":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Reporting a Vulnerability"},"3206":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#supported-versions","content":"Security fixes are provided for the latest minor release of `travels`."},"3207":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Please report security issues privately by opening a GitHub security advisory for this repository. Do not file public issues for vulnerabilities."},"3208":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Include:"},"3209":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"affected version"},"3210":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"reproduction steps"},"3211":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"impact and affected APIs"},"3212":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"any known workaround"},"3213":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Maintainers will acknowledge valid reports as soon as practical, triage severity, and publish a patched release when needed."},"3214":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing Strategy","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing"},"3215":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing","content":"Correctness, property-based, browser, mutation, and hot-path performance testing."},"3216":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"Mutation smoke test"},"3217":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"Hot-path budgets"},"3218":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing","content":"Travels combines example-based, property-based, browser, package-consumer, coverage, and mutation smoke tests."},"3219":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"Run:"},"3220":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"The smoke suite temporarily introduces a small set of high-value correctness regressions and verifies that focused tests fail. Every source file is restored in a `finally` block. The mutations cover backward replay ordering, controlled journal patch-pair validation, and mutable transaction rollback completeness."},"3221":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"This is intentionally a deterministic gate rather than a broad probabilistic mutation campaign. Add a mutation whenever a bug fix depends on a subtle operator, boundary, or rollback step that line coverage alone would not protect."},"3222":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"Run:"},"3223":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"The matrix benchmark guards `setState` throughput and serialized history size. It does not cover undo/redo navigation or the controlled journal, and a change that made controlled navigation 53x slower and external commits 5.5x slower than the 2.1.0 line passed it unnoticed."},"3224":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"`benchmarks/hot-path-check.js` measures per-operation cost for `setState`, navigation, transactions, and both controlled-journal paths, and fails the build when one exceeds its budget. The budgets are order-of-magnitude smoke limits, set far above the measured cost so shared CI runners do not flake; each scenario takes the best of three runs for the same reason. They are not percent-level drift detectors. Tighten a budget only alongside a measured improvement, and add a scenario whenever a new operation joins the timeline's hot path."},"3225":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting"},"3226":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose common update, navigation, persistence, mutable-mode, and integration problems."},"3227":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"An update does not appear in history"},"3228":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Undo or redo buttons stay stale"},"3229":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#instanceof-travels-fails-or-throws","content":"`instanceof Travels` fails or throws"},"3230":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"A restored snapshot throws"},"3231":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"JSON persistence loses values"},"3232":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"A mutable store loses or unexpectedly changes its root reference"},"3233":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"A transaction did not roll everything back"},"3234":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#observer-errors-or-reentrant-mutations","content":"Observer errors or reentrant mutations"},"3235":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Controlled journal history diverges from the owner"},"3236":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#the-website-needs-a-markdown-or-llm-version","content":"The website needs a Markdown or LLM version"},"3237":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#still-stuck","content":"Still stuck?"},"3238":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","content":"Use the sections below to isolate whether a problem belongs to state ownership, history recording, replay, persistence, or the UI binding. Stable error and warning codes are listed in Error Handling."},"3239":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"Check these conditions in order:"},"3240":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Did the value actually change?** No-op patch groups create no entry and no event."},"3241":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Is `autoArchive: false` enabled?** Pending updates need `archive()` or an operation that implicitly archives them."},"3242":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Is tracking paused?** Resume it in a `finally` block."},"3243":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Are you writing through Travels?** Direct assignments to `getState()`, a MobX/Vue store, or another owner are not recorded."},"3244":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Are you using a controlled journal?** Call `recordPatches()` with the owner’s exact patch pair; journals intentionally omit `setState()`."},"3245":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Did an updater throw or return a Promise?** Keep callbacks synchronous and await data before calling them."},"3246":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"Use `getRevision()` to verify whether a committed event occurred and `subscribe()` to inspect the event type."},"3247":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"State identity is not enough to invalidate controls. `archive()` and `rebase()` can change the timeline without replacing state."},"3248":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"In React, subscribe with `useSyncExternalStore(travels.subscribe, travels.getRevision)`."},"3249":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"In another store, mirror `getRevision()` or relevant controls after every committed event."},"3250":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Confirm the subscription was not disposed prematurely."},"3251":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Do not create a new timeline on every component render."},"3252":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"See Navigation and Controls."},"3253":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#instanceof-travels-fails-or-throws","content":"The exported `Travels` value is a persistence namespace, not a constructor in Travels 3. Create instances with `createTravels()` and detect them with `isTravels(value)`. Controlled journals are not state-owning Travels instances and return `false` from that guard."},"3254":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Parse storage before assuming its shape; `Travels.deserialize()` accepts JSON strings or parsed objects."},"3255":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Use `validation: 'semantic'` for unverified input so invalid replay is detected at restore."},"3256":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Match `strict` and `mark` through `replayOptions` when they were customized during recording."},"3257":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Migrate older application and history shapes before validation."},"3258":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Check `TravelsPersistenceError.code`, plus `entryIndex` and `direction` when present."},"3259":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Supply a known-safe `fallback` for intentional startup recovery."},"3260":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Do not pass separate `history`, `initialPatches`, or `initialPosition` options in v3. Pass one complete snapshot to `restoreTravels()`."},"3261":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"JSON does not preserve `undefined`, `bigint`, `NaN`, infinities, `-0`, prototypes, Map/Set, circular references, or shared object identity. Some values throw; others are silently converted or dropped."},"3262":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"Run:"},"3263":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"Then inspect the reported path and normalize the value according to State Requirements. Remember that an incompatible value can remain in an old patch after leaving current state."},"3264":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"Check whether the operation replaced the root, used a primitive root, or navigated through a root-replacement patch. Prefer localized draft mutations. For restore, pass the observed object as `target` with `mutable: true`:"},"3265":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"Do not combine mutable mode with `enableAutoFreeze`. Read the complete operation identity table."},"3266":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"Travels rolls back writes made through its own APIs. It cannot roll back direct mutable-store assignments, network requests, DOM changes, storage writes, or other external side effects."},"3267":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"Move every undoable state write into `setState()`, keep the callback synchronous, and manage external side effects after successful commit or with a separate compensation strategy. Framework observers attached directly to mutable state can also see provisional writes even though Travels observers cannot."},"3268":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#observer-errors-or-reentrant-mutations","content":"Observers run after commit. They cannot veto or safely mutate the same transition. Schedule follow-up work in a later task and avoid cycles. Use `onObserverError` to isolate listener/devtools failures; an observer exception does not roll back the state that already committed."},"3269":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Record the exact post-commit state and exact forward/inverse pair from the same transition."},"3270":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Do not rerun the recipe inside Travels."},"3271":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Do not record navigation triggered by `apply` as a new edit."},"3272":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Make `apply` synchronous and return the state actually committed."},"3273":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Handle root replacement explicitly when applying patches in place."},"3274":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Preflight with `assertTravelHistoryEntryRecordable()` when the owner cannot roll back a published commit."},"3275":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Travels validates patch structure but deliberately does not regenerate patches to prove the owner’s transition. That relationship belongs to the adapter."},"3276":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#the-website-